1
00:00:00,141 --> 00:00:05,908
[Filing For Love]

2
00:00:10,177 --> 00:00:12,543
[Yeonhyang Temple Food Experience, 2013]

3
00:00:37,779 --> 00:00:40,340
[The late Lady, Joo Kyung Hee]

4
00:00:45,518 --> 00:00:49,024
Mom, the air's nice up here.

5
00:01:07,811 --> 00:01:11,614
<i>Hey! Please untie me! Hurry!</i>

6
00:01:11,614 --> 00:01:12,705
<i>What are you doing?</i>

7
00:01:12,705 --> 00:01:14,911
<i>Please untie me already!</i>

8
00:01:14,911 --> 00:01:16,898
<i>I need to get out of here!</i>

9
00:01:16,898 --> 00:01:18,125
<i>Mom!</i>

10
00:01:18,125 --> 00:01:20,135
<i>- I need to get out of here!
- Mom!</i>

11
00:01:20,135 --> 00:01:22,304
<i>Let me go!</i>

12
00:01:22,304 --> 00:01:25,217
<i>What are you doing?</i>

13
00:01:25,217 --> 00:01:26,537
<i>No!</i>

14
00:01:26,537 --> 00:01:28,395
<i>No!</i>

15
00:01:35,862 --> 00:01:39,013
If you jump from there,
you'll just inconvenience people.

16
00:01:40,882 --> 00:01:43,520
The hiking trail's right below you.

17
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:47,170
Man, it must've taken a lot
to climb all the way up here.

18
00:01:47,170 --> 00:01:51,211
Why not use that same willpower
to keep living instead?

19
00:01:51,211 --> 00:01:55,336
Just enjoy the fresh air and head down.
The way down's a lot nicer anyway.

20
00:02:12,991 --> 00:02:16,224
I think the buses stopped running.

21
00:02:17,054 --> 00:02:19,772
Seriously? No way...

22
00:02:19,772 --> 00:02:21,612
Where are you headed?

23
00:02:21,612 --> 00:02:22,706
I'll give you a ride.

24
00:02:22,706 --> 00:02:25,027
I'm not getting in a car with a guy
who almost jumped off a cliff.

25
00:02:25,027 --> 00:02:26,392
That's terrifying.

26
00:02:26,392 --> 00:02:28,550
No thanks.

27
00:02:29,238 --> 00:02:31,448
Fair point.

28
00:02:33,352 --> 00:02:35,602
Hey.

29
00:02:35,602 --> 00:02:37,914
Let's meet again sometime. Alive.

30
00:02:54,541 --> 00:02:58,092
Hello, I'm Lee Tae Kwon, one of the new hires.

31
00:02:58,092 --> 00:03:00,538
Looking forward to working with you all.

32
00:03:02,495 --> 00:03:03,705
And lastly,

33
00:03:03,705 --> 00:03:09,312
Joo In Ah here actually came in first
in this recruitment round.

34
00:03:09,312 --> 00:03:10,822
Total elite.

35
00:03:10,822 --> 00:03:12,327
I'll do my best to live up to it.

36
00:03:12,327 --> 00:03:13,951
Looking forward to working with you.

37
00:03:13,951 --> 00:03:15,760
Thank you.

38
00:03:33,042 --> 00:03:36,342
Why are you two so quiet?

39
00:03:37,807 --> 00:03:41,386
In Ah, you should pour Manager Jeon a drink.

40
00:03:41,386 --> 00:03:43,280
Oh, okay.

41
00:04:08,461 --> 00:04:11,218
I heard you're the Haemu Group prince.

42
00:04:11,218 --> 00:04:14,331
The legendary third-gen chaebol himself.

43
00:04:16,228 --> 00:04:20,267
Then I guess you also heard
I'm not exactly royalty.

44
00:04:22,634 --> 00:04:24,372
So...

45
00:04:24,372 --> 00:04:27,117
that's what made life so hard for you
back then?

46
00:04:28,951 --> 00:04:30,567
Anyway, let's work well together.

47
00:04:30,567 --> 00:04:32,863
Manager Jeon Jae Yeol.

48
00:04:40,046 --> 00:04:42,390
I really hoped I'd see you again.

49
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:46,280
Good thing I stayed alive.

50
00:04:56,872 --> 00:04:58,821
What do you mean?

51
00:04:58,821 --> 00:05:02,223
Jae Yeol handled this project
from the very beginning.

52
00:05:02,223 --> 00:05:05,187
All that's left is the signature,
and now you're taking his credit away?

53
00:05:05,187 --> 00:05:08,847
In Ah, read the room.

54
00:05:08,847 --> 00:05:14,014
Ever since Jeon Seong Yeol joined,
they've been funneling all the wins his way.

55
00:05:14,014 --> 00:05:17,170
So what? That makes it okay?

56
00:05:17,826 --> 00:05:20,619
- If the Chairman finds out...
- Come on.

57
00:05:20,619 --> 00:05:24,632
This only works because
the Chairman's letting it happen.

58
00:05:26,351 --> 00:05:28,108
You heard about

59
00:05:28,108 --> 00:05:29,721
Jeon Jae Yeol's mother too, right?

60
00:05:29,721 --> 00:05:31,438
People think he has limitations.

61
00:05:31,438 --> 00:05:34,688
That's why everyone's siding
with the second son no matter what.

62
00:05:34,688 --> 00:05:37,303
Go to Dubai and close the deal.
There's a flight in two hours.

63
00:05:37,303 --> 00:05:40,278
- Seriously, you need to hurry.
- In Ah.

64
00:05:40,278 --> 00:05:43,104
You're going to get yourself in trouble.

65
00:05:43,104 --> 00:05:46,516
And this isn't my project.

66
00:05:46,516 --> 00:05:48,929
It's the company's project.

67
00:05:49,775 --> 00:05:51,453
Still, this is so unfair.

68
00:05:51,453 --> 00:05:54,822
You did all the work.

69
00:05:54,822 --> 00:05:57,329
It's enough that you know that.

70
00:06:04,212 --> 00:06:09,035
They're seriously the worst.
Every single one of them.

71
00:06:09,035 --> 00:06:10,895
In Ah.

72
00:06:13,915 --> 00:06:15,828
I'm going to

73
00:06:16,602 --> 00:06:19,465
protect you in this company.

74
00:06:19,465 --> 00:06:22,471
Come hell or high water,

75
00:06:24,555 --> 00:06:27,461
I'm standing by you, Jeon Jae Yeol.

76
00:06:32,628 --> 00:06:35,391
This pisses me off.

77
00:06:48,263 --> 00:06:50,491
So... you two used to date.

78
00:06:52,144 --> 00:06:54,711
Yeah. We did.

79
00:06:57,364 --> 00:06:59,571
Why'd you break up?

80
00:07:00,330 --> 00:07:02,122
Well...

81
00:07:02,122 --> 00:07:05,768
He found someone more suitable for his world,

82
00:07:05,768 --> 00:07:08,098
and I wanted to live my own life.

83
00:07:08,098 --> 00:07:10,185
Same old story.

84
00:07:10,185 --> 00:07:12,069
It's all in the past.

85
00:07:12,885 --> 00:07:14,647
You sure about that?

86
00:07:15,702 --> 00:07:17,623
What do you mean?

87
00:07:25,205 --> 00:07:27,230
We got a tip.

88
00:07:27,230 --> 00:07:30,723
That you were involved
in an inappropriate relationship at work.

89
00:07:30,723 --> 00:07:34,489
Those photos were of you two, huh?
You and the Vice Chairman.

90
00:08:01,554 --> 00:08:02,781
<i>You came.</i>

91
00:08:02,781 --> 00:08:04,833
<i>It's been a while,</i>

92
00:08:04,833 --> 00:08:06,278
<i>Vice Chairman.</i>

93
00:08:10,752 --> 00:08:13,172
<i>I missed you.</i>

94
00:08:16,084 --> 00:08:19,487
It was the day he came back from overseas.

95
00:08:19,487 --> 00:08:22,787
It was just a hug after seeing him again.
It meant nothing.

96
00:08:25,158 --> 00:08:27,663
"It meant nothing?"

97
00:08:27,663 --> 00:08:32,825
That's not really what I saw back there.

98
00:08:34,029 --> 00:08:37,934
Are those feelings one-sided
on the Vice Chairman's part?

99
00:08:37,934 --> 00:08:39,582
Or do you two

100
00:08:40,250 --> 00:08:42,910
still have feelings for each other?

101
00:09:09,621 --> 00:09:12,794
<i>I'd appreciate it if you stopped
showing up uninvited.</i>

102
00:09:14,866 --> 00:09:15,896
<i>In Ah.</i>

103
00:09:15,896 --> 00:09:17,160
<i>Let go.</i>

104
00:09:18,072 --> 00:09:20,033
<i>Let go!</i>

105
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:30,719
The Vice Chairman and I are just coworkers.

106
00:09:30,719 --> 00:09:32,659
Nothing more, nothing less.

107
00:09:32,659 --> 00:09:35,525
I don't have feelings for him anymore.

108
00:09:41,782 --> 00:09:44,440
Honestly, after we got the tip,
I was suspicious.

109
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:47,604
So I looked into you, followed you around,

110
00:09:47,604 --> 00:09:50,083
even staked out your place.

111
00:09:52,961 --> 00:09:54,434
Figures.

112
00:09:54,434 --> 00:09:55,936
Living up to your reputation as Audit's Ace.

113
00:09:55,936 --> 00:09:59,626
Didn't expect it to be the Vice Chairman,
though.

114
00:10:00,747 --> 00:10:02,434
So?

115
00:10:03,690 --> 00:10:07,028
What's your conclusion as the PM lead?

116
00:10:16,354 --> 00:10:18,208
I don't know.

117
00:10:19,641 --> 00:10:22,397
I want to believe

118
00:10:22,397 --> 00:10:24,971
everything you said.

119
00:10:25,761 --> 00:10:27,572
That you two are over.

120
00:10:27,572 --> 00:10:30,858
No matter how he feels,

121
00:10:30,858 --> 00:10:33,549
you don't have feelings for him anymore.

122
00:10:33,549 --> 00:10:34,918
But maybe

123
00:10:36,209 --> 00:10:39,542
that's just me wanting to believe that.

124
00:10:45,050 --> 00:10:47,701
Just give me some time.

125
00:10:47,701 --> 00:10:50,414
I'll try to think about this objectively.

126
00:11:35,805 --> 00:11:40,099
[Episode 7: To Her Lover]

127
00:11:44,224 --> 00:11:46,514
- Five soju glasses.
- Five soju glasses.

128
00:11:46,514 --> 00:11:49,274
- And five paper cups too.
- Five.

129
00:11:49,274 --> 00:11:51,871
- Two spoons.
- Oh, sparkling water.

130
00:11:51,871 --> 00:11:53,181
Sparkling water?

131
00:11:53,181 --> 00:11:54,568
- Didn't add that.
- For highballs.

132
00:11:54,568 --> 00:11:57,362
Okay. Add sparkling water too, please.

133
00:11:57,362 --> 00:11:59,109
Yeah, and...

134
00:11:59,109 --> 00:12:03,189
Sir, why do you keep pacing around?
I'm already losing my mind here.

135
00:12:03,189 --> 00:12:06,566
You know, it's our first workshop in forever.

136
00:12:06,566 --> 00:12:08,397
I was thinking,

137
00:12:08,397 --> 00:12:11,677
this workshop really needs some barbecue.

138
00:12:11,677 --> 00:12:13,354
Otherwise it'll feel kind of lame.

139
00:12:13,354 --> 00:12:16,076
- Don't you think so, White Blood Cell?
- Yes, it would be a little disappointing.

140
00:12:16,076 --> 00:12:16,743
- Right?
- Yeah.

141
00:12:16,743 --> 00:12:17,918
Unnie,

142
00:12:17,918 --> 00:12:21,052
11 people are driving themselves,
and everyone else is taking the bus.

143
00:12:21,052 --> 00:12:22,302
Okay.

144
00:12:22,302 --> 00:12:25,026
Then send that list to the driver.

145
00:12:25,026 --> 00:12:26,183
Got it.

146
00:12:26,183 --> 00:12:29,511
Since when were you two on "unnie" terms?

147
00:12:29,511 --> 00:12:31,464
Funny what you pick up on.

148
00:12:31,464 --> 00:12:33,694
Did you finish everything you needed to do?

149
00:12:33,694 --> 00:12:35,034
Why are you still here?

150
00:12:35,034 --> 00:12:37,223
Did you text the whole Audit team or not?

151
00:12:37,223 --> 00:12:40,569
I'm doing it now, unnie. Quit nagging already.

152
00:12:40,569 --> 00:12:44,293
Hae Young, I really think we need
whole pork belly or pork neck.

153
00:12:44,293 --> 00:12:46,063
- Okay, okay.
- Should we buy some then?

154
00:12:46,063 --> 00:12:49,866
- I'll get pork neck.
- Great, buy the whole cut.

155
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:18,107
Assistant Manager Noh Ki Jun, was it?

156
00:13:18,107 --> 00:13:19,884
Can he be trusted?

157
00:13:19,884 --> 00:13:21,902
He seemed pretty cocky.

158
00:13:23,780 --> 00:13:26,902
Yeah, he's definitely not the obedient type.

159
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:29,950
What did he mean earlier?

160
00:13:29,950 --> 00:13:31,974
"The thing you call impossible,
it's not so impossible after all."

161
00:13:31,974 --> 00:13:34,291
What was impossible again...

162
00:13:34,291 --> 00:13:36,350
and what wasn't?

163
00:13:37,922 --> 00:13:40,526
Why is the Vice Chairman of Haemu Group

164
00:13:40,526 --> 00:13:42,745
so interested in some random assistant manager?

165
00:13:42,745 --> 00:13:45,390
Shouldn't you have bigger things
to worry about?

166
00:14:07,967 --> 00:14:09,481
Ma'am.

167
00:14:09,481 --> 00:14:10,528
Yeah, Hae Young?

168
00:14:10,528 --> 00:14:12,317
They're replacing all the company cards.

169
00:14:12,317 --> 00:14:14,238
If you give me yours,
I'll dispose of it for you.

170
00:14:14,238 --> 00:14:17,278
- It's in my bag. I'll bring it to you.
- Okay, thanks.

171
00:14:32,477 --> 00:14:34,800
<i>See?</i>

172
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:37,310
<i>The thing you call impossible...</i>

173
00:14:37,310 --> 00:14:39,575
<i>it's not so impossible after all.</i>

174
00:15:00,474 --> 00:15:03,311
Do we really need to wait
until the next board meeting for this?

175
00:15:03,311 --> 00:15:05,161
It may still be a little premature.

176
00:15:05,161 --> 00:15:08,387
Though of course,
your opinion matters most, sir.

177
00:15:10,044 --> 00:15:12,901
You said you met with MD Han, right?

178
00:15:12,901 --> 00:15:14,170
Yes, I did.

179
00:15:25,511 --> 00:15:27,330
Noh Ki Jun!

180
00:15:27,330 --> 00:15:29,330
Hey, knock first.

181
00:15:30,086 --> 00:15:32,016
I'm making ramen. Want some?

182
00:15:32,016 --> 00:15:33,403
No.

183
00:15:33,403 --> 00:15:35,035
You better not ask for a bite later.

184
00:15:35,035 --> 00:15:36,534
Hey, Ah Jeong.

185
00:15:38,256 --> 00:15:40,033
Your Vice Chairman...

186
00:15:40,033 --> 00:15:41,868
What kind of person is he?

187
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:45,537
Why are you calling him "your" Vice Chairman?

188
00:15:45,537 --> 00:15:47,908
He's yours too.

189
00:15:49,336 --> 00:15:51,206
Right.

190
00:15:51,206 --> 00:15:52,566
He was my boss.

191
00:15:52,566 --> 00:15:54,749
Why are you suddenly asking about him?

192
00:15:54,749 --> 00:15:59,096
I thought you were stressing over Joo In Ah.

193
00:15:59,096 --> 00:16:01,593
You stormed out
saying you were going to figure out

194
00:16:01,593 --> 00:16:04,346
what was going on between you two.

195
00:16:05,045 --> 00:16:06,288
So? Did you?

196
00:16:06,288 --> 00:16:08,808
I did figure out one thing.

197
00:16:09,471 --> 00:16:11,936
She's insanely hard to read.

198
00:16:11,936 --> 00:16:12,961
What does that mean?

199
00:16:12,961 --> 00:16:14,782
Never mind.

200
00:16:14,782 --> 00:16:16,772
Enjoy your ramen.

201
00:16:19,048 --> 00:16:20,569
What the...

202
00:16:42,781 --> 00:16:45,426
[2025 Haemu Strategic Planning Division
Joint Workshop]

203
00:17:00,934 --> 00:17:03,153
Oh, we're having barbecue?

204
00:17:03,177 --> 00:17:06,467
Yeah, a workshop isn't a workshop
without barbecue.

205
00:17:06,467 --> 00:17:09,691
Team Leader Moo, you've got taste.

206
00:17:09,691 --> 00:17:11,788
Let me help carry some too.

207
00:17:11,788 --> 00:17:13,076
No, this thing's heavy.

208
00:17:13,076 --> 00:17:16,581
Let me show you the charm of
a down-to-earth boss.

209
00:17:17,180 --> 00:17:20,496
This has got to weigh like 20 kilos.
She's so strong.

210
00:17:20,496 --> 00:17:21,877
- Hey, put it down already.
- Okay.

211
00:17:21,877 --> 00:17:23,338
Let's go.

212
00:17:32,072 --> 00:17:34,878
There you go again, acting tough.

213
00:17:42,676 --> 00:17:45,123
[Strategic Planning Division Joint Workshop]

214
00:17:45,124 --> 00:17:46,934
The Planning Office,

215
00:17:46,934 --> 00:17:48,958
HR,

216
00:17:48,958 --> 00:17:50,871
and Audit.

217
00:17:52,078 --> 00:17:55,581
Wow, just hearing those names
sounds intimidating already.

218
00:17:57,741 --> 00:18:01,208
Thank you all for carrying
the weight of this company.

219
00:18:01,208 --> 00:18:03,298
At least during this workshop,

220
00:18:03,298 --> 00:18:07,714
I hope you forget all the work you left behind
and just enjoy yourselves.

221
00:18:19,439 --> 00:18:20,727
<i>Hi, Daddy.</i>

222
00:18:20,727 --> 00:18:22,046
Hold on.

223
00:18:22,046 --> 00:18:25,430
Why are you still awake?
Isn't it almost midnight over there?

224
00:18:25,430 --> 00:18:28,027
<i>I'm tired. Mom nags too much.</i>

225
00:18:28,027 --> 00:18:30,364
Hey, listen to your mom.

226
00:18:30,364 --> 00:18:33,092
She's been getting headaches lately.

227
00:18:33,092 --> 00:18:34,136
Got it?

228
00:18:34,136 --> 00:18:36,368
Go to sleep now. We'll talk again tomorrow.

229
00:18:36,368 --> 00:18:37,430
Good night.

230
00:18:37,430 --> 00:18:39,726
<i>Good night.</i>

231
00:18:39,726 --> 00:18:41,089
Mr. Ahn,

232
00:18:41,089 --> 00:18:43,071
you should take some time off soon

233
00:18:43,071 --> 00:18:45,289
and visit your family in the States.

234
00:18:45,289 --> 00:18:47,509
I didn't realize you were here, sir.

235
00:18:47,509 --> 00:18:49,131
You have a lovely family.

236
00:18:49,131 --> 00:18:51,223
Are the others at the next activity already?

237
00:18:51,223 --> 00:18:54,287
We originally planned some team-building games,

238
00:18:54,287 --> 00:18:58,973
but the two chiefs said
sports are the best way to build teamwork.

239
00:19:00,452 --> 00:19:03,680
[2025 Strategic Planning Division
Joint Workshop]

240
00:19:07,262 --> 00:19:09,402
- Stretch properly.
- Yeah.

241
00:19:13,989 --> 00:19:16,224
I thought we'd just watch
training videos or something.

242
00:19:16,224 --> 00:19:17,714
Why futsal?

243
00:19:17,714 --> 00:19:20,157
Ms. Yoon, didn't you hear?

244
00:19:20,157 --> 00:19:24,273
Ms. Joo said today's MVP
doesn't have to come to work tomorrow.

245
00:19:29,870 --> 00:19:31,656
What are you doing?

246
00:19:34,387 --> 00:19:36,073
Look at her.

247
00:19:37,247 --> 00:19:39,720
Wow, you're really into this.

248
00:19:41,008 --> 00:19:42,806
Faster! Faster!

249
00:19:42,806 --> 00:19:45,212
Guess you don't work out much.

250
00:19:45,826 --> 00:19:47,523
Alright!

251
00:19:47,523 --> 00:19:50,578
It's a co-ed match,
so be careful not to get hurt!

252
00:19:50,578 --> 00:19:53,737
- Got it!
- No sliding tackles!

253
00:19:53,737 --> 00:19:55,739
Let's keep the contact light
and make safety the priority!

254
00:19:55,739 --> 00:19:56,541
Got it!

255
00:19:56,541 --> 00:20:00,060
What does that matter in competition?
Winning's all that counts.

256
00:20:00,060 --> 00:20:02,245
Here, have one before you play.

257
00:20:02,245 --> 00:20:04,282
Time for some energy investing.

258
00:20:04,282 --> 00:20:05,321
Thanks.

259
00:20:05,321 --> 00:20:06,593
- Energy investing?
- Thank you.

260
00:20:06,593 --> 00:20:08,219
Energy's an asset too.

261
00:20:08,219 --> 00:20:11,580
You save it up like investments,
then use it when you need it.

262
00:20:11,580 --> 00:20:14,222
- Thank you.
- Like right now.

263
00:20:17,897 --> 00:20:19,443
Thanks.

264
00:20:21,766 --> 00:20:23,600
Oh, thank you.

265
00:20:30,031 --> 00:20:32,442
Hey, what's going on here?

266
00:20:32,442 --> 00:20:34,560
Why are only your people
getting the good stuff?

267
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:36,220
Isn't this cheating?

268
00:20:36,220 --> 00:20:38,697
It is, right?

269
00:20:38,697 --> 00:20:39,995
Hello.

270
00:20:39,995 --> 00:20:41,461
- Hello, sir.
- Hello, sir.

271
00:20:41,461 --> 00:20:43,406
Hello.

272
00:20:43,406 --> 00:20:45,129
Oh, Vice Chairman.

273
00:20:45,129 --> 00:20:48,002
I thought you left after the welcome speech.

274
00:20:48,002 --> 00:20:50,772
I heard things were getting fun,
so I came to cheer you on.

275
00:20:50,772 --> 00:20:53,559
Then you're rooting for the Audit, right?

276
00:20:53,559 --> 00:20:55,215
What? No way!

277
00:20:55,215 --> 00:20:56,890
You're on HR's side, right?

278
00:20:56,890 --> 00:21:00,647
Well... maybe I'll side with whoever wins.

279
00:21:02,868 --> 00:21:05,298
Then you're on Audit's side.

280
00:21:05,298 --> 00:21:07,204
That's boring.

281
00:21:10,139 --> 00:21:14,418
Isn't it lame to avoid competition
and just side with the stronger team?

282
00:21:18,827 --> 00:21:22,538
You say that like
you're already the stronger one.

283
00:21:22,538 --> 00:21:24,011
Maybe I am.

284
00:21:25,017 --> 00:21:27,690
Because I'm going to win.

285
00:21:30,928 --> 00:21:35,061
Assistant Manager Noh is
a little too competitive sometimes.

286
00:21:35,902 --> 00:21:38,759
Guess we won't be on the same side then.

287
00:21:38,759 --> 00:21:41,149
How about we go head-to-head?

288
00:21:41,149 --> 00:21:43,899
Sir, you're actually playing?

289
00:21:43,899 --> 00:21:46,099
You have a meeting at three.

290
00:21:46,099 --> 00:21:47,992
Cancel it.

291
00:22:36,107 --> 00:22:38,026
Vice Chairman!

292
00:22:38,026 --> 00:22:39,861
Oh no, are you okay?

293
00:22:39,861 --> 00:22:41,154
You alright?

294
00:22:41,154 --> 00:22:43,698
I told you to take it easy! Oh my...

295
00:22:43,698 --> 00:22:46,842
What's with him? Did he lose his mind?

296
00:22:46,842 --> 00:22:49,412
Guess he's trying to win MVP.
So he can skip work tomorrow.

297
00:22:49,412 --> 00:22:52,227
At this rate, he'll be off work forever.

298
00:22:52,227 --> 00:22:54,125
That must be uncomfortable.
Wear my sneakers instead.

299
00:22:54,125 --> 00:22:54,811
It's okay.

300
00:22:54,811 --> 00:22:57,548
- Put these on.
- Thanks.

301
00:22:58,165 --> 00:23:00,909
Better than playing in dress shoes.

302
00:23:22,402 --> 00:23:23,975
What the hell? Hey, foul!

303
00:23:23,975 --> 00:23:25,393
- Ref!
- No foul!

304
00:23:25,393 --> 00:23:27,705
- What?
- No. That wasn't a foul.

305
00:23:27,705 --> 00:23:29,744
That was just physical play.

306
00:23:29,744 --> 00:23:31,996
- Go, go!
- That was excessive...

307
00:23:31,996 --> 00:23:34,332
- Vice Chairman, shoot!
- Hold on, timeout!

308
00:23:34,332 --> 00:23:35,797
Timeout, timeout!

309
00:23:35,797 --> 00:23:38,920
Shoot! Shoot! Shoot!

310
00:23:38,920 --> 00:23:40,841
Timeout! Timeout!

311
00:23:40,841 --> 00:23:44,676
You got that on camera, right? You filmed it.

312
00:23:44,676 --> 00:23:46,386
Ref! VAR! VAR!

313
00:23:46,386 --> 00:23:47,667
Boo, Ki Jun!

314
00:23:47,667 --> 00:23:49,984
Please! VAR!

315
00:23:49,984 --> 00:23:52,058
- VAR please!
- What a sore loser!

316
00:23:52,058 --> 00:23:53,399
Pathetic. So lame.

317
00:23:53,399 --> 00:23:55,505
Playing dirty too.

318
00:24:12,245 --> 00:24:14,958
Alright, back on offense!

319
00:24:49,525 --> 00:24:51,442
You okay?

320
00:24:59,019 --> 00:25:01,544
You were so sure you'd win.

321
00:25:02,183 --> 00:25:03,903
Must be disappointing.

322
00:25:05,076 --> 00:25:07,612
Not really. We didn't exactly play fair.

323
00:25:10,657 --> 00:25:13,873
I'll apologize on In Ah's behalf

324
00:25:13,873 --> 00:25:16,467
for tripping you on purpose.

325
00:25:16,467 --> 00:25:18,956
That's just the kind of person she is.

326
00:25:20,980 --> 00:25:23,160
And what kind of person is that?

327
00:25:24,950 --> 00:25:26,746
Maybe her legs were just too long.

328
00:25:28,037 --> 00:25:30,854
Don't you have someone like that too?

329
00:25:30,854 --> 00:25:33,827
Someone who's always on your side.

330
00:25:35,862 --> 00:25:38,969
In Ah and I go way back.

331
00:25:43,710 --> 00:25:45,223
Sir,

332
00:25:46,001 --> 00:25:48,069
are you feeling guilty about something?

333
00:25:49,096 --> 00:25:51,793
You keep overexplaining yourself.

334
00:25:51,793 --> 00:25:54,897
Makes it seem like
you've got something to hide from me.

335
00:26:12,368 --> 00:26:15,425
Director Choi brought
a change of clothes for you.

336
00:26:15,425 --> 00:26:18,024
Should I adjust your dinner schedule too?

337
00:26:20,012 --> 00:26:22,108
<i>I'm living</i>

338
00:26:22,108 --> 00:26:24,209
<i>with a guy right now.</i>

339
00:26:27,590 --> 00:26:29,590
Secretary Park.

340
00:26:30,518 --> 00:26:34,231
That guy you said you were living with...

341
00:26:35,372 --> 00:26:38,478
Is it Assistant Manager Noh Ki Jun?

342
00:26:54,909 --> 00:26:56,601
Gosh.

343
00:26:59,289 --> 00:27:01,755
Are you going to break it?

344
00:27:03,099 --> 00:27:04,632
Come here.

345
00:27:10,142 --> 00:27:11,554
Sit down.

346
00:27:17,900 --> 00:27:20,139
- Was it this side?
- Gosh, you scared me!

347
00:27:22,312 --> 00:27:24,258
It's this ankle.

348
00:27:25,246 --> 00:27:27,373
- Let me see.
- I'm fine...

349
00:27:30,114 --> 00:27:32,318
It's barely even swollen.

350
00:27:32,318 --> 00:27:34,085
What?

351
00:27:34,085 --> 00:27:37,169
Look.
My ankles are usually way thinner than this.

352
00:27:37,169 --> 00:27:38,871
Such a baby.

353
00:27:40,776 --> 00:27:43,921
First you hurt me, now you're playing nurse?

354
00:27:43,921 --> 00:27:46,016
You tripped me on purpose earlier, huh?

355
00:27:46,016 --> 00:27:48,019
How could you do that to your own teammate?

356
00:27:48,019 --> 00:27:51,653
So what if he missed a goal?
It's not the end of the world.

357
00:27:51,653 --> 00:27:53,677
You must be really worried about him.

358
00:27:53,677 --> 00:27:57,570
If you'd pushed it any further,
your career here would've been over.

359
00:27:57,570 --> 00:27:59,901
In front of all those employees,
especially HR...

360
00:27:59,901 --> 00:28:02,220
Why do you push it so far?

361
00:28:02,220 --> 00:28:06,020
Even if he let it slide,
everyone else would've bowed to him anyway.

362
00:28:07,943 --> 00:28:10,894
You've been in corporate life
long enough to know better.

363
00:28:10,894 --> 00:28:12,939
Why are you acting like a kid?

364
00:28:17,768 --> 00:28:19,658
So you are on my side?

365
00:28:19,658 --> 00:28:21,439
Not the Vice Chairman's?

366
00:28:22,325 --> 00:28:23,855
It's not about sides.

367
00:28:23,855 --> 00:28:28,058
I was just protecting my employee as your boss.

368
00:28:37,677 --> 00:28:38,798
Okay.

369
00:28:38,798 --> 00:28:39,887
What's "okay?"

370
00:28:39,887 --> 00:28:41,962
Your case.

371
00:28:41,962 --> 00:28:43,996
I think I can close it now.

372
00:28:43,996 --> 00:28:45,018
All of a sudden?

373
00:28:45,018 --> 00:28:49,486
When the people involved deny it,
and there's no clear evidence,

374
00:28:49,486 --> 00:28:52,780
these cases usually get closed
without disciplinary action.

375
00:28:52,780 --> 00:28:54,703
I kept wondering if I should dig deeper,

376
00:28:54,703 --> 00:28:58,409
or if I needed to sit down and question

377
00:28:58,409 --> 00:29:00,409
the Vice Chairman himself.

378
00:29:02,482 --> 00:29:05,229
But after today, I think I finally get it.

379
00:29:06,429 --> 00:29:08,746
You two

380
00:29:08,746 --> 00:29:11,509
aren't on the same page at all.

381
00:29:15,536 --> 00:29:16,991
I believe you.

382
00:29:18,250 --> 00:29:20,155
I want to believe

383
00:29:21,976 --> 00:29:23,507
how you feel.

384
00:29:27,835 --> 00:29:29,499
And how exactly

385
00:29:31,021 --> 00:29:32,483
do I feel?

386
00:29:37,077 --> 00:29:40,204
Was today really just about

387
00:29:40,833 --> 00:29:44,389
protecting your employee?

388
00:29:51,570 --> 00:29:54,362
I showed you already.

389
00:29:54,362 --> 00:29:56,601
Nothing's impossible.

390
00:29:57,783 --> 00:30:00,593
I don't care if it takes time.

391
00:30:00,593 --> 00:30:03,606
Take a good look at your feelings.

392
00:30:05,279 --> 00:30:07,218
I'll wait.

393
00:30:26,192 --> 00:30:28,328
So while you were showering,

394
00:30:28,328 --> 00:30:31,588
someone filmed inside the shower room?

395
00:30:31,588 --> 00:30:35,428
Yeah, I'm sure he was filming me with a phone.

396
00:30:35,428 --> 00:30:37,359
Did you see what the guy looked like?

397
00:30:37,359 --> 00:30:39,423
Anything?

398
00:30:39,423 --> 00:30:42,428
I only caught a glimpse of his back,

399
00:30:45,058 --> 00:30:48,330
but he was wearing
our division's men's T-shirt.

400
00:30:51,297 --> 00:30:53,114
Disgusting.

401
00:30:54,986 --> 00:30:57,133
So it was someone from inside.

402
00:30:58,013 --> 00:31:00,477
And since this is the lodging area,
there aren't any security cameras.

403
00:31:00,477 --> 00:31:02,821
Is there anything else you remember?

404
00:31:02,821 --> 00:31:05,711
I think he was using a white phone.

405
00:31:05,711 --> 00:31:09,424
What I saw was white and rectangular.

406
00:31:16,407 --> 00:31:18,417
I think

407
00:31:18,417 --> 00:31:20,887
this could be resolved pretty easily,

408
00:31:21,847 --> 00:31:24,698
if the male employees cooperate.

409
00:31:24,698 --> 00:31:26,304
So you want to check everyone's phones?

410
00:31:26,304 --> 00:31:30,135
Let's only check the phones
belonging to people with white phones.

411
00:31:30,135 --> 00:31:32,852
The suspect could've hidden the phone he used,

412
00:31:32,852 --> 00:31:35,648
so I think we should search all the rooms too.

413
00:31:38,311 --> 00:31:39,692
That's a little much...

414
00:31:39,692 --> 00:31:42,572
I still think we need to verify things first.

415
00:31:44,110 --> 00:31:46,502
I know this is uncomfortable,
but please bear with us.

416
00:31:46,502 --> 00:31:48,793
- Of course.
- We should absolutely do it.

417
00:31:48,793 --> 00:31:52,013
But we can't rule out the possibility
that the suspect is someone from Audit.

418
00:31:52,013 --> 00:31:54,768
So to keep things fair,
let's have one representative from HR

419
00:31:54,768 --> 00:31:56,966
and one from Audit check only what's necessary.

420
00:31:56,966 --> 00:31:58,985
Sounds good.

421
00:31:58,985 --> 00:32:01,589
General Manager Ahn, you can handle it for HR.

422
00:32:01,589 --> 00:32:05,341
If someone like you handles it,
I don't think anyone will complain.

423
00:32:05,341 --> 00:32:07,307
Okay, got it.

424
00:32:24,860 --> 00:32:27,426
- Oh, you...
- Sir, actually...

425
00:32:29,348 --> 00:32:31,658
You two look good together.

426
00:32:31,658 --> 00:32:34,308
- I'll pretend I didn't see anything.
- Thank you.

427
00:32:48,320 --> 00:32:50,517
Come on...

428
00:32:50,517 --> 00:32:53,747
You're with Audit. How can you be doing this?

429
00:33:02,200 --> 00:33:03,960
This is...

430
00:33:05,159 --> 00:33:08,092
This is leftover sauce from the barbecue...

431
00:33:11,404 --> 00:33:14,501
No, let's just give it to him.
It's already been opened anyway.

432
00:33:14,501 --> 00:33:16,501
Take it home and eat it.

433
00:33:17,814 --> 00:33:19,207
Thanks.

434
00:33:30,144 --> 00:33:33,055
Just in case,
we checked all the women's rooms too,

435
00:33:33,055 --> 00:33:34,778
but nothing turned up.

436
00:33:34,778 --> 00:33:37,403
Still, we should do everything we can.

437
00:33:39,561 --> 00:33:42,352
Maybe there are security cameras
near the entrance?

438
00:33:42,352 --> 00:33:43,716
Once it gets light tomorrow,

439
00:33:43,716 --> 00:33:46,838
I'll ask the Operations Team
and check right away.

440
00:33:46,838 --> 00:33:49,256
Anyway, everyone worked hard tonight.

441
00:33:49,256 --> 00:33:51,361
Let's all get some rest.

442
00:33:51,361 --> 00:33:53,134
Good work, everyone.

443
00:33:57,079 --> 00:33:58,269
Mr. Ahn,

444
00:33:58,269 --> 00:34:00,017
you dropped this.

445
00:34:03,130 --> 00:34:04,660
You smoke?

446
00:34:04,660 --> 00:34:06,166
Since when?

447
00:34:07,473 --> 00:34:08,943
Yeah, just occasionally.

448
00:34:08,943 --> 00:34:10,664
I keep it on the down-low.

449
00:34:10,664 --> 00:34:13,531
Why are you sneaking cigarettes even at work?

450
00:34:13,531 --> 00:34:15,741
Want to step outside for a smoke together?

451
00:34:15,741 --> 00:34:18,501
<i>I think he was using a white phone.</i>

452
00:34:18,501 --> 00:34:20,691
No, it's okay. I'm quitting soon anyway.

453
00:34:20,691 --> 00:34:22,646
Thanks. Give it here.

454
00:34:22,646 --> 00:34:24,733
- I'm not giving it back.
- Why not?

455
00:34:24,733 --> 00:34:26,943
If you're really quitting,
you should start now.

456
00:34:26,943 --> 00:34:28,172
I'll help you out.

457
00:34:28,172 --> 00:34:30,821
No, I'll quit starting tomorrow.

458
00:34:30,821 --> 00:34:32,713
Stuff like this only works
if you quit cold turkey.

459
00:34:32,713 --> 00:34:35,219
Mr. Noh, don't give it back.

460
00:34:35,219 --> 00:34:36,457
Yes, ma'am.

461
00:34:36,457 --> 00:34:38,588
Come on, you guys are ruthless.

462
00:34:38,588 --> 00:34:39,986
Just give it back already!

463
00:34:39,986 --> 00:34:43,292
Seriously.
Why are you messing with the man's cigarettes?

464
00:34:43,292 --> 00:34:45,194
Those things are expensive now.

465
00:34:45,194 --> 00:34:46,574
Exactly.

466
00:34:47,179 --> 00:34:48,840
Yeah?

467
00:35:08,736 --> 00:35:10,335
What the...

468
00:35:11,643 --> 00:35:15,255
What? What is it?

469
00:35:17,191 --> 00:35:19,826
Isn't this a camera?

470
00:35:22,619 --> 00:35:24,417
Mr. Ahn!

471
00:35:24,417 --> 00:35:26,421
Jesus Christ.

472
00:35:29,507 --> 00:35:32,440
You've lost your mind!

473
00:35:41,308 --> 00:35:44,462
You really went all out.

474
00:35:44,462 --> 00:35:47,468
Anytime, anywhere, huh?

475
00:35:47,468 --> 00:35:49,278
From the elevator on the way to work,

476
00:35:49,278 --> 00:35:52,332
to the office cafeteria, the bathroom,

477
00:35:52,332 --> 00:35:54,458
even the subway ride home.

478
00:35:55,825 --> 00:35:57,528
How did you even take this one...

479
00:36:00,418 --> 00:36:01,745
No way.

480
00:36:01,745 --> 00:36:05,365
Did you install cameras under employees' desks?

481
00:36:05,365 --> 00:36:07,489
This angle is way too low.

482
00:36:07,489 --> 00:36:09,115
Ma'am, you know...

483
00:36:09,115 --> 00:36:13,599
How could you do this to people
you see every single day?

484
00:36:13,599 --> 00:36:16,317
What the hell do you even think
your coworkers are?

485
00:36:16,317 --> 00:36:18,597
Okay, I get it, but...

486
00:36:19,470 --> 00:36:21,880
Everyone's cooperating, aren't they?

487
00:36:21,880 --> 00:36:25,644
Making a huge scene out of this
won't help the company either.

488
00:36:25,644 --> 00:36:27,980
There's already the issue
with suspicion falling on our division,

489
00:36:27,980 --> 00:36:30,733
- and the company's image...
- Right. That's important.

490
00:36:30,733 --> 00:36:33,569
The division's reputation. The company's image.

491
00:36:33,569 --> 00:36:35,265
Which is exactly why...

492
00:36:40,986 --> 00:36:43,010
we should make an example out of this.

493
00:36:43,010 --> 00:36:45,483
Then this is the perfect chance
to prove we're better

494
00:36:45,483 --> 00:36:49,947
than those companies that cover up

495
00:36:49,947 --> 00:36:51,893
workplace sex crimes.

496
00:37:09,952 --> 00:37:11,850
Today...

497
00:37:11,850 --> 00:37:14,596
I'm eating at the cafeteria.

498
00:37:15,203 --> 00:37:17,739
Okay, I'll let them know.

499
00:37:17,739 --> 00:37:19,669
No.

500
00:37:19,669 --> 00:37:21,831
Let's just head down now.

501
00:37:26,212 --> 00:37:28,250
I told you, I don't eat cafeteria food.

502
00:37:28,250 --> 00:37:31,396
Just eat already so we can wrap up
General Manager Ahn's report.

503
00:37:31,396 --> 00:37:32,545
Eat.

504
00:37:32,545 --> 00:37:35,257
Come on, good food boosts productivity.

505
00:37:35,257 --> 00:37:37,288
That's how you get good reports.

506
00:37:38,444 --> 00:37:40,448
It's good though.

507
00:37:40,448 --> 00:37:41,889
It's tasty.

508
00:37:48,805 --> 00:37:50,373
What the...

509
00:37:52,963 --> 00:37:54,897
Mind if I join you?

510
00:37:55,783 --> 00:37:58,273
Sure. It's not like we reserved the place.

511
00:37:58,273 --> 00:37:59,873
Have a seat.

512
00:38:13,100 --> 00:38:14,628
Jae Yeol went to the cafeteria?

513
00:38:14,628 --> 00:38:15,688
Yes.

514
00:38:15,688 --> 00:38:19,763
And he sat with our Head of Audit
and Mr. Noh from Audit Team 3.

515
00:38:19,763 --> 00:38:22,342
The whole Audit is freaking out.

516
00:38:23,470 --> 00:38:27,787
Man, my brother's sneakier than he looks.

517
00:38:27,787 --> 00:38:30,613
Well, I've got Audit Team 1's finest, huh?

518
00:38:30,613 --> 00:38:32,613
I've got you on my side.

519
00:38:34,296 --> 00:38:36,790
I'm honored, sir.

520
00:38:37,894 --> 00:38:39,528
So how's work these days?

521
00:38:39,528 --> 00:38:42,052
You're handling affiliate audits now, right?

522
00:38:42,052 --> 00:38:45,332
Yes, I'm currently in charge
of Steel and Pharma.

523
00:38:47,607 --> 00:38:50,045
Oh, you're handling Pharma?

524
00:38:50,045 --> 00:38:52,684
Who was in charge before you?

525
00:38:54,261 --> 00:38:58,533
May I ask why you're asking?

526
00:38:58,533 --> 00:39:01,216
Oh, it's nothing serious.

527
00:39:01,216 --> 00:39:03,676
I had drinks with some people
from Pharma yesterday,

528
00:39:03,676 --> 00:39:06,646
and they said HQ Audit
used to be all over them,

529
00:39:06,646 --> 00:39:09,518
but things have gone quiet lately.

530
00:39:09,518 --> 00:39:12,461
So I was wondering
if the old team was power-tripping,

531
00:39:12,461 --> 00:39:15,994
or if things just weren't being handled
properly now.

532
00:39:15,994 --> 00:39:18,152
Guess it was because
the person in charge changed.

533
00:39:18,152 --> 00:39:19,652
I see.

534
00:39:29,465 --> 00:39:32,036
I heard you played a big role

535
00:39:32,036 --> 00:39:34,215
in catching the illegal filming suspect.

536
00:39:34,215 --> 00:39:37,115
Well, I was just doing my job.

537
00:39:37,758 --> 00:39:41,377
Seems like a capable employee.
So why are you wasting him on PM work?

538
00:39:45,177 --> 00:39:48,981
I'm good at pretty much everything.

539
00:39:54,760 --> 00:39:56,333
This is good.

540
00:40:27,909 --> 00:40:30,232
You two...

541
00:40:30,232 --> 00:40:33,072
are close, aren't you?

542
00:40:33,072 --> 00:40:35,477
I happened to see you together

543
00:40:35,477 --> 00:40:38,423
when I dropped her off the other day.

544
00:40:39,940 --> 00:40:41,608
Is it rude to bring up
personal matters like this

545
00:40:41,608 --> 00:40:44,695
in front of your direct supervisor?

546
00:40:44,695 --> 00:40:46,919
Yes. It is rude.

547
00:40:49,350 --> 00:40:50,951
And what's wrong with it anyway?

548
00:40:50,951 --> 00:40:52,617
Housing prices in Seoul are insane.

549
00:40:52,617 --> 00:40:54,277
It's economical.

550
00:40:55,285 --> 00:40:57,435
You knew about this?

551
00:40:57,435 --> 00:40:59,008
Of course.

552
00:40:59,738 --> 00:41:03,125
Head Joo's even been to our place before.

553
00:41:07,290 --> 00:41:08,750
Really?

554
00:41:12,107 --> 00:41:16,267
Since when did this company
start doing home visits?

555
00:41:25,522 --> 00:41:29,045
I should probably get going.

556
00:41:29,045 --> 00:41:31,015
I was in the middle of something.

557
00:41:31,015 --> 00:41:32,803
Sit down.

558
00:41:32,803 --> 00:41:34,746
We sat at the same table.

559
00:41:34,746 --> 00:41:37,546
Isn't it rude to leave first?

560
00:41:39,965 --> 00:41:41,935
The Vice Chairman's right.

561
00:41:41,935 --> 00:41:43,562
Let's go together, Mr. Noh.

562
00:41:43,562 --> 00:41:46,245
I almost let you leave alone. How rude of me.

563
00:41:46,245 --> 00:41:49,604
We were eating together originally.

564
00:41:49,604 --> 00:41:51,470
Then enjoy your meal, you two.

565
00:41:51,470 --> 00:41:52,892
Let's go.

566
00:41:54,859 --> 00:41:56,991
Come on, hurry up.

567
00:42:09,231 --> 00:42:12,115
- This is good, right?
- Yeah.

568
00:42:12,115 --> 00:42:15,338
I hate wasting food, but it couldn't be helped.

569
00:42:15,338 --> 00:42:17,295
Such a waste.

570
00:42:17,295 --> 00:42:19,715
By the way, this toast is amazing.

571
00:42:19,715 --> 00:42:23,212
First time trying it?
That place has been famous forever.

572
00:42:23,212 --> 00:42:24,516
Back when I was a rookie,

573
00:42:24,516 --> 00:42:26,541
buying one of these on the way to work
and eating it at my desk

574
00:42:26,541 --> 00:42:28,592
was the highlight of my day.

575
00:42:28,592 --> 00:42:31,012
Did you buy one for the Vice Chairman too?

576
00:42:31,012 --> 00:42:32,562
Who knows?

577
00:42:35,453 --> 00:42:38,437
He must've been pissed. Right?

578
00:42:38,437 --> 00:42:41,537
How am I supposed to survive at work now?

579
00:42:42,217 --> 00:42:45,181
Are you going to take responsibility
and protect your employee?

580
00:42:45,181 --> 00:42:47,960
Who told you to act out like that?

581
00:42:47,960 --> 00:42:52,120
Come on,
the Vice Chairman was being ridiculously petty.

582
00:42:53,106 --> 00:42:54,658
Anyway, after today,

583
00:42:54,658 --> 00:42:57,369
it's pretty obvious he's still not over you.

584
00:42:57,369 --> 00:42:59,371
Want to reopen the investigation then?

585
00:42:59,371 --> 00:43:00,423
No.

586
00:43:00,423 --> 00:43:02,675
As long as you're not the problem,
I don't care.

587
00:43:03,501 --> 00:43:05,544
Some people just hold onto their first love.

588
00:43:05,544 --> 00:43:08,820
Like the rose from The Little Prince.

589
00:43:11,553 --> 00:43:14,595
- What's that supposed to mean?
- You know...

590
00:43:14,595 --> 00:43:18,924
Even after the Little Prince comes to Earth
and sees all those identical roses,

591
00:43:18,924 --> 00:43:22,764
he still goes back to the planet with his rose.

592
00:43:23,715 --> 00:43:26,206
The Little Prince goes back?

593
00:43:26,206 --> 00:43:27,608
Doesn't he stay on Earth with the fox?

594
00:43:27,608 --> 00:43:30,510
No, he goes back.

595
00:43:30,510 --> 00:43:32,404
He says he has to take responsibility
for the rose he raised.

596
00:43:32,404 --> 00:43:34,527
No, he stays on Earth.

597
00:43:34,527 --> 00:43:36,202
No, he goes back.

598
00:43:36,202 --> 00:43:37,853
Want to bet on it?

599
00:43:38,474 --> 00:43:39,625
A bet?

600
00:43:39,625 --> 00:43:40,662
Deal.

601
00:43:40,662 --> 00:43:43,376
But no wish bet. Loser gets punished.

602
00:43:43,376 --> 00:43:44,442
Fine.

603
00:43:45,087 --> 00:43:47,488
"I'll be going back to my star tonight."

604
00:43:47,488 --> 00:43:50,154
See? He goes back to his planet.

605
00:43:51,535 --> 00:43:53,887
What the heck? This is actually really sad.

606
00:43:53,887 --> 00:43:56,770
Why did I remember it as a happy ending?

607
00:43:56,770 --> 00:43:59,964
Guess you just interpreted it
as a happy ending back then.

608
00:44:00,557 --> 00:44:02,017
If he made it all the way to Earth,

609
00:44:02,017 --> 00:44:04,362
why go through all that trouble
just to leave again?

610
00:44:07,408 --> 00:44:09,003
So I win, right?

611
00:44:09,619 --> 00:44:13,418
Hey, you really took
children's books seriously, huh?

612
00:44:14,247 --> 00:44:18,180
Just admit defeat gracefully
and take your punishment.

613
00:44:18,898 --> 00:44:22,029
Fine, I admit it. What's the punishment?

614
00:44:22,029 --> 00:44:23,285
Okay.

615
00:44:24,323 --> 00:44:26,600
Now what should we do here

616
00:44:26,600 --> 00:44:29,152
to turn this into a tragic fairy tale?

617
00:44:40,847 --> 00:44:42,847
What are you plotting?

618
00:45:02,369 --> 00:45:05,012
Head Joo finally put something in her hair.

619
00:45:10,520 --> 00:45:12,473
Ma'am...

620
00:45:14,447 --> 00:45:16,191
Your hair...

621
00:45:18,966 --> 00:45:20,598
What?

622
00:45:22,013 --> 00:45:24,016
Isn't it cute?

623
00:45:24,016 --> 00:45:26,938
I'm totally obsessed
with stuff like this lately.

624
00:45:33,114 --> 00:45:35,174
Alright, show's over.

625
00:45:49,959 --> 00:45:54,181
[Art Class Director]

626
00:45:57,083 --> 00:45:58,526
Thank you.

627
00:45:58,526 --> 00:45:59,971
That's cute.

628
00:45:59,971 --> 00:46:02,591
What's with the hairpin?

629
00:46:02,591 --> 00:46:05,583
Oh right. I still had this on?

630
00:46:06,303 --> 00:46:07,961
This is so embarrassing.

631
00:46:07,961 --> 00:46:09,457
Well, that's unusual.

632
00:46:09,457 --> 00:46:10,897
Is it trendy these days?

633
00:46:10,897 --> 00:46:14,280
No, someone just gave it to me.

634
00:46:14,906 --> 00:46:16,699
It's a punishment.

635
00:46:20,067 --> 00:46:21,555
Anyway,

636
00:46:22,144 --> 00:46:24,481
you're saying I shouldn't model anymore?

637
00:46:24,481 --> 00:46:26,021
What, am I fired?

638
00:46:26,021 --> 00:46:28,799
We should really be using pro models now.

639
00:46:28,799 --> 00:46:32,718
I've been shamelessly using you
because of budget issues.

640
00:46:32,718 --> 00:46:36,441
Oh, come on. I did it because I wanted to.

641
00:46:36,441 --> 00:46:39,528
And you know that. I needed this.

642
00:46:39,528 --> 00:46:41,626
Do you still?

643
00:46:44,027 --> 00:46:47,498
I've known you a long time, In Ah.

644
00:46:47,498 --> 00:46:48,728
Lately, I've been thinking

645
00:46:48,728 --> 00:46:53,144
maybe you don't need this place
as much anymore.

646
00:46:54,041 --> 00:46:55,706
You've been smiling a lot.

647
00:46:57,131 --> 00:46:58,441
- Me?
- Yeah.

648
00:46:58,441 --> 00:47:00,441
You seem relaxed.

649
00:47:01,044 --> 00:47:02,694
Tell me.

650
00:47:02,694 --> 00:47:04,495
There's someone, isn't there?

651
00:47:04,495 --> 00:47:06,747
The guy who gave you that pin?

652
00:47:09,340 --> 00:47:12,332
<i>No, this is just...</i>

653
00:47:12,332 --> 00:47:14,120
<i>Since you're the flower of our Audit Team,</i>

654
00:47:14,120 --> 00:47:15,512
<i>how about adding an actual flower?</i>

655
00:47:15,512 --> 00:47:17,104
<i>Here.</i>

656
00:47:18,924 --> 00:47:20,572
<i>Pig.</i>

657
00:47:20,572 --> 00:47:23,061
<i>And rabbit.</i>

658
00:47:23,061 --> 00:47:25,010
<i>Look to the side.</i>

659
00:47:28,697 --> 00:47:29,909
I can't do that.

660
00:47:29,909 --> 00:47:32,575
What do you mean, you can't?

661
00:47:33,545 --> 00:47:35,604
He works at my company.

662
00:47:36,622 --> 00:47:40,882
There's a saying overseas about office dating.

663
00:47:40,882 --> 00:47:43,401
"Don't crap where you eat."

664
00:47:44,749 --> 00:47:46,419
That's how crazy it is.

665
00:47:46,419 --> 00:47:48,269
So what?

666
00:47:48,269 --> 00:47:50,416
Isn't that better than bottling everything up?

667
00:47:50,416 --> 00:47:54,326
What's wrong with doing
something a little crazy?

668
00:47:54,326 --> 00:47:58,494
Before you started modeling,
didn't you think this was crazy too?

669
00:47:58,494 --> 00:47:59,883
But once you tried it,

670
00:47:59,883 --> 00:48:03,011
it became the one escape
from your everyday life.

671
00:48:03,011 --> 00:48:05,337
Don't box yourself in.

672
00:48:05,337 --> 00:48:07,012
Once you step outside those limits,

673
00:48:07,012 --> 00:48:09,475
that's when new happiness finds you.

674
00:48:11,260 --> 00:48:13,703
Wow, you sound wise today.

675
00:48:13,703 --> 00:48:15,836
You just realized?

676
00:48:39,006 --> 00:48:42,043
[Art Class Today: 9 PM]

677
00:48:57,068 --> 00:48:59,454
<i>Was I this pretty?</i>

678
00:49:11,742 --> 00:49:14,375
<i>Yeah, you are.</i>

679
00:49:38,523 --> 00:49:41,303
[Audit Report]

680
00:49:46,548 --> 00:49:48,852
You barely touched your lunch.

681
00:49:48,852 --> 00:49:50,604
Please eat something.

682
00:49:51,888 --> 00:49:53,365
Okay.

683
00:49:53,365 --> 00:49:55,875
And you went too far earlier.

684
00:49:58,041 --> 00:50:00,845
You totally used me.

685
00:50:00,845 --> 00:50:02,970
I know

686
00:50:02,970 --> 00:50:05,414
you like Head Joo.

687
00:50:07,848 --> 00:50:11,167
I'm a very capable secretary.

688
00:50:11,167 --> 00:50:13,599
I'm also a woman who likes you.

689
00:50:15,683 --> 00:50:17,708
Ki Jun is...

690
00:50:17,708 --> 00:50:19,927
a really great guy.

691
00:50:20,899 --> 00:50:24,857
For the first time in my life,
I hated someone seeing me at my worst,

692
00:50:24,857 --> 00:50:27,993
and ran away
because I didn't want to burden him.

693
00:50:27,993 --> 00:50:31,131
I didn't want to look pathetic in front of him.

694
00:50:38,936 --> 00:50:40,520
Why are you telling me this?

695
00:50:40,520 --> 00:50:43,773
Because that's how impossible it is.
For you to beat Ki Jun.

696
00:50:45,205 --> 00:50:47,328
Even if you are the Vice Chairman.

697
00:51:05,316 --> 00:51:08,461
[Report Regarding
U.S. Assignment Personnel Changes]

698
00:51:23,926 --> 00:51:26,263
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

699
00:51:26,263 --> 00:51:27,970
- Two toast sandwiches, please.
- Sure.

700
00:51:27,970 --> 00:51:29,970
- Please make them good.
- Of course.

701
00:51:31,644 --> 00:51:34,439
- Enjoy your food.
- Thank you.

702
00:51:40,435 --> 00:51:42,400
Beats me.

703
00:51:42,400 --> 00:51:44,156
What could he possibly have left to say?

704
00:51:44,156 --> 00:51:45,607
[General Manager Ahn (Pervert)]

705
00:51:52,091 --> 00:51:55,486
<i>The person you're calling is unavailable.
Please leave a message...</i>

706
00:51:55,486 --> 00:51:56,743
[Assistant Manager Noh Ki Jun]

707
00:52:02,726 --> 00:52:04,712
Come on, pick up.

708
00:52:19,912 --> 00:52:21,510
Hey, Noh Ki Jun!

709
00:52:21,510 --> 00:52:22,942
What are you, seriously?

710
00:52:22,942 --> 00:52:25,202
You really got yourself
on the Vice Chairman's good side, huh?

711
00:52:25,202 --> 00:52:26,534
What are you talking about?

712
00:52:26,534 --> 00:52:28,344
I heard it all from HR.

713
00:52:28,344 --> 00:52:30,460
You're getting sent to the U.S., right?

714
00:52:31,537 --> 00:52:32,694
What?

715
00:52:33,830 --> 00:52:35,449
Lucky you.

716
00:52:38,450 --> 00:52:41,430
<i>The person you're calling is unavailable...</i>

717
00:52:45,409 --> 00:52:47,961
Assistant Manager Lee.

718
00:52:47,961 --> 00:52:50,527
Thanks for coming out even though you're busy.

719
00:52:57,284 --> 00:52:59,422
You're putting me in a difficult position too.

720
00:52:59,422 --> 00:53:01,931
You know I'm in deep trouble right now.

721
00:53:01,931 --> 00:53:03,973
My wife is about to divorce me.

722
00:53:03,973 --> 00:53:05,826
She says...

723
00:53:07,945 --> 00:53:10,951
I can forget about ever seeing my son again.

724
00:53:12,584 --> 00:53:13,701
Please...

725
00:53:13,701 --> 00:53:15,207
Help me.

726
00:53:15,207 --> 00:53:19,412
Can't you help me get a lighter punishment?

727
00:53:19,412 --> 00:53:23,835
Tell them I worked hard all these years,
that I had a good reputation.

728
00:53:23,835 --> 00:53:27,108
Maybe get the employees
to write petitions for me too.

729
00:53:27,108 --> 00:53:30,745
Even if I wanted to help personally,

730
00:53:30,745 --> 00:53:33,554
Audit's taking this really seriously.

731
00:53:33,554 --> 00:53:34,979
You know...

732
00:53:34,979 --> 00:53:38,769
I've been trying to get ahold
of Assistant Manager Noh too,

733
00:53:38,769 --> 00:53:41,008
but he won't answer.

734
00:53:41,709 --> 00:53:42,919
Sir,

735
00:53:42,919 --> 00:53:44,984
he's riding high right now.

736
00:53:44,984 --> 00:53:47,450
He got recognized because of your case,
he's getting promoted,

737
00:53:47,450 --> 00:53:49,886
and now he's even going to the U.S. assignment.

738
00:53:50,641 --> 00:53:52,641
You didn't know?

739
00:53:54,068 --> 00:53:55,519
Director Park,

740
00:53:55,519 --> 00:53:57,946
I heard your daughter's getting married.

741
00:53:57,946 --> 00:53:59,576
Congratulations.

742
00:53:59,576 --> 00:54:01,816
Let me know once the date's set.

743
00:54:01,816 --> 00:54:03,326
I'd love to give a speech.

744
00:54:03,326 --> 00:54:06,396
Wow, that wedding's going to be huge.

745
00:54:06,396 --> 00:54:07,508
Oh my...

746
00:54:07,508 --> 00:54:11,695
You'd personally attend and even give a speech?

747
00:54:11,695 --> 00:54:14,431
Or should I sing instead?

748
00:54:33,205 --> 00:54:35,902
<i>The person you're calling is unavailable...</i>

749
00:54:35,902 --> 00:54:37,155
Why isn't she answering?

750
00:54:37,155 --> 00:54:38,106
[Joo In Ah]

751
00:54:42,441 --> 00:54:44,564
<i>The person you're calling is unavailable...</i>

752
00:54:46,729 --> 00:54:49,628
Hey, have you seen Head Joo?

753
00:54:50,395 --> 00:54:52,072
I'm asking if you've seen her.

754
00:54:52,072 --> 00:54:55,126
I didn't see it myself,
but Seung Hee just told me.

755
00:54:55,126 --> 00:54:58,517
Head Joo suddenly showed up,
then left with the Vice Chairman.

756
00:54:59,654 --> 00:55:01,053
Where'd they go?

757
00:55:04,711 --> 00:55:06,342
- What are you trying to do?
- What do you mean?

758
00:55:06,342 --> 00:55:07,875
About Noh Ki Jun.

759
00:55:07,875 --> 00:55:11,055
How do you ship him off overnight

760
00:55:11,055 --> 00:55:12,675
without even giving us a heads-up?

761
00:55:12,675 --> 00:55:15,193
What is he, some kind of package?

762
00:55:15,193 --> 00:55:19,066
So that's why you barged in here?

763
00:55:19,712 --> 00:55:21,871
In the middle of an executive meeting?

764
00:55:21,871 --> 00:55:23,840
Over one assistant manager?

765
00:55:23,840 --> 00:55:25,598
This isn't just about him.

766
00:55:25,598 --> 00:55:28,840
This is about respecting my role and authority.

767
00:55:28,840 --> 00:55:32,936
How do you transfer someone
with zero disciplinary issues like this?

768
00:55:34,804 --> 00:55:37,047
This is completely unfair.

769
00:55:37,047 --> 00:55:39,318
Honestly, it's audit-worthy.

770
00:55:39,318 --> 00:55:41,201
I reviewed everything.

771
00:55:41,201 --> 00:55:44,686
A capable employee with great results
doing nothing but PM work?

772
00:55:44,686 --> 00:55:46,686
That's a loss for the company.

773
00:55:48,933 --> 00:55:50,933
That's really the reason?

774
00:55:52,231 --> 00:55:54,746
This has nothing to do with personal feelings?

775
00:55:55,637 --> 00:55:57,001
It's a U.S. assignment.

776
00:55:57,001 --> 00:55:59,794
Every employee wants a posting like that.

777
00:55:59,794 --> 00:56:02,024
For someone at his level,
it's basically special treatment.

778
00:56:02,024 --> 00:56:04,142
He's getting promoted to manager too.

779
00:56:04,142 --> 00:56:06,585
Is this really worth getting upset over?

780
00:56:06,585 --> 00:56:07,955
Or are you the one

781
00:56:07,955 --> 00:56:12,894
letting personal feelings
hold back a promising employee's career?

782
00:56:13,829 --> 00:56:16,192
Can you honestly say

783
00:56:16,192 --> 00:56:19,165
you're upset for purely professional reasons?

784
00:56:23,853 --> 00:56:26,040
In Ah.

785
00:56:26,040 --> 00:56:28,640
I had a lot of options.

786
00:56:29,506 --> 00:56:33,369
And I chose the most considerate one.

787
00:56:40,959 --> 00:56:43,032
<i>The person you're calling is unavailable...</i>

788
00:56:44,499 --> 00:56:46,171
Noh Ki Jun.

789
00:56:49,722 --> 00:56:51,268
Mr. Ahn?

790
00:56:53,242 --> 00:56:56,432
You can't keep showing up like this
and calling me...

791
00:57:03,228 --> 00:57:05,228
You bastard...

792
00:58:20,542 --> 00:58:23,655
You can't drive like this. I'll take you.

793
00:58:41,109 --> 00:58:43,489
So they're still waiting at the ER?

794
00:58:46,653 --> 00:58:49,383
No, you don't have to. I'll call again later.

795
00:58:49,383 --> 00:58:51,433
Just let me out here.

796
00:58:51,433 --> 00:58:53,624
You're still pretty far.
Just past the intersection...

797
00:58:53,624 --> 00:58:56,402
In Ah... In Ah!

798
00:59:11,887 --> 00:59:14,133
<i>It just hurts.</i>

799
00:59:17,967 --> 00:59:20,146
<i>Feels like you must've been really lonely.</i>

800
00:59:22,830 --> 00:59:25,358
<i>You keep acting tough,</i>

801
00:59:27,159 --> 00:59:29,545
<i>and that just makes it sadder.</i>

802
00:59:34,503 --> 00:59:37,823
<i>But let me ask you one thing.</i>

803
00:59:45,660 --> 00:59:48,473
<i>Why are you pushing me away this hard?</i>

804
01:00:01,237 --> 01:00:03,849
<i>That question you asked me...</i>

805
01:00:04,689 --> 01:00:07,876
<i>Why I really keep pushing you away...</i>

806
01:00:12,159 --> 01:00:13,597
<i>I...</i>

807
01:00:16,946 --> 01:00:18,457
<i>I...</i>

808
01:00:22,261 --> 01:00:25,253
[Filing For Love]

809
01:00:53,816 --> 01:00:54,857
<i>Mr. Noh...</i>

810
01:00:54,857 --> 01:00:56,580
<i>I was scared. It scared me.</i>

811
01:00:56,580 --> 01:01:00,001
<i>You can go with us
on the Jeju business trip next week.</i>

812
01:01:00,001 --> 01:01:01,264
<i>What the hell are you doing?</i>

813
01:01:01,264 --> 01:01:03,921
<i>You sent him overseas because of your feelings.</i>

814
01:01:03,921 --> 01:01:06,428
<i>In Ah, just stay by my side.</i>

815
01:01:06,428 --> 01:01:09,565
<i>Why did you really send me to Team 3?</i>

816
01:01:09,565 --> 01:01:11,155
<i>Because you were afraid he might get hurt?</i>

817
01:01:11,155 --> 01:01:13,655
<i>None of this makes any sense to me.</i>

818
01:01:13,655 --> 01:01:15,912
<i>Talk to me. Right now.</i>

819
01:01:15,912 --> 01:01:17,182
<i>I'm weird like that.</i>

820
01:01:17,182 --> 01:01:20,842
<i>When it really matters, I hide how I feel.</i>
